        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mondamin%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was platted in the winter of 1867–1868 when the railroad reached the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mondamin%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Spooner‑Holeton House was built in 1870 and stands as one of the town's oldest structures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://home.nps.gov/places/mondamin-iowa.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Over its 150‑year history, the Spooner‑Holeton House has served as a drug store, private residence, and library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://home.nps.gov/places/mondamin-iowa.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Spooner‑Holeton House now functions as a museum furnished in an 1880s style.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://home.nps.gov/places/mondamin-iowa.htm",
